It builds on the following MIT-licensed works:

- Videowright by Scott Cosman (https://github.com/scosman/videowright):
  render/vw.ts is derived from videowright 0.1.1 (with the layout-check
  additions described in its header), and the example project layout follows
  its project conventions.
- tiny-video-renderer by the same author: the CDP-screenshot-to-ffmpeg
  pipeline that Videowright itself builds on.

Command-line behaviour of some utilities (gap/padding/colour naming) follows
Tailwind CSS's 4px scale conventions; no Tailwind code is included.

The narration stack used at runtime (installed by setup.sh into a local venv,
not distributed with this kit):
- Kokoro-82M TTS and its misaki phonemizer
- OpenAI Whisper (openai-whisper) for transcript verification

The bundled themes/motion-engineering theme is the "Motion Engineering" style
originally published as part of Videowright's example set, with its embedded
Space Grotesk and JetBrains Mono webfonts.
